{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.PivotalCategory","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PivotalCategory","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Rigid.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Rigid.Braided","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.RightDualIsoUnique","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.RigidTensorDual"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.drinfeldIso_naturality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.drinfeldIso_naturality","kind":"theorem","line":337,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PivotalCategory.lean#L337-L344","doc":"**Naturality of the Drinfeld isomorphism.**  `rightAdjointMate_congr_dual` compares the two\nduals of `Xᘁ`; `swap_mate_mate` identifies the mate taken against the swapped pairings with `f`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.swap_mate_mate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.swap_mate_mate","kind":"theorem","line":314,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PivotalCategory.lean#L314-L335","doc":"**Taking the mate twice, the second time against the swapped pairings, is the identity.**\n\nThe braided form of Mathlib's \"Future work\" entry *\"Show that the left adjoint mate of the right\nadjoint mate of a morphism is the morphism itself.\"*\n\nBoth `(fᘁ)ᘁ` and `f` satisfy the same identity against the evaluation — for `f` by braiding\nnaturality on each side plus `rightAdjointMate_comp_evaluation` — and pairing against the\nevaluation is injective. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.swapRightDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.swapRightDual","kind":"def","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PivotalCategory.lean#L307-L312","doc":"`X` as a right dual **of** `Xᘁ`, via `BraidedCategory.exactPairing_swap`.  Deliberately a `def`\nand not an instance: `Xᘁ` already has a right dual from `RightRigidCategory`, and this is the other\none. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.rightAdjointMate_congr_dual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.rightAdjointMate_congr_dual","kind":"theorem","line":287,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PivotalCategory.lean#L287-L300","doc":"**The right adjoint mate does not depend on the choice of duals**, up to `rightDualIso`.\n\nBoth sides are the *mixed* mate — taken with `X`'s second dual and `Y`'s first — reached by\n`comp_rightAdjointMate` with explicit instance arguments, composing `f` with an identity on either\nside.  Mathlib has no naturality lemma for `rightDualIso`; `rightDualIso_id` is the only one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.drinfeldIso","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.drinfeldIso","kind":"def","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PivotalCategory.lean#L268-L278","doc":"**In a braided right-rigid category every object is isomorphic to its double dual**,\n`X ≅ Xᘁᘁ` — the Drinfeld isomorphism.\n\nThe argument is uniqueness of duals, twice over.  `X` and `Xᘁ` form an exact pairing by rigidity;\n`BraidedCategory.exactPairing_swap` turns that pairing around, so `X` is a right dual **of** `Xᘁ`.\nBut `Xᘁᘁ` is the chosen right dual of `Xᘁ`, and right duals are unique up to canonical isomorphism\n(`rightDualIso`).\n\nPointwise and unconditional; its naturality is `drinfeldIso_naturality` below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PivotalCategory.ofPointwise","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PivotalCategory.ofPointwise","kind":"def","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PivotalCategory.lean#L250-L260","doc":"**Build a pivotal structure from object-wise data.**  A choice of `X ≅ Xᘁᘁ` for each `X`, plus\nthe naturality square, *is* a natural isomorphism `𝟭 C ≅ ᘁᘁ`.  Together with `pivotor_naturality`\nthis says the two presentations carry the same data, so a proof in either style lands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PivotalCategory.pivotorApp_tensor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PivotalCategory.pivotorApp_tensor","kind":"theorem","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PivotalCategory.lean#L242-L246","doc":"**Monoidality of the pivotor**, object-wise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PivotalCategory.pivotor_naturality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PivotalCategory.pivotor_naturality","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PivotalCategory.lean#L236-L240","doc":"**Naturality of the pivotor**, object-wise: it commutes with the double mate.  This is the form\na string-diagram argument produces, and it is exactly `NatTrans.naturality` for `pivotor`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PivotalCategory.pivotorApp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PivotalCategory.pivotorApp","kind":"def","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PivotalCategory.lean#L233-L234","doc":"The pivotor at an object: `X ≅ Xᘁᘁ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PivotalCategory.pivotor_tensor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PivotalCategory.pivotor_tensor","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PivotalCategory.lean#L221-L221","doc":"**Monoidality**: the pivotor is compatible with `⊗`, measured against the comparison\n`(X ⊗ Y)ᘁᘁ ≅ Xᘁᘁ ⊗ Yᘁᘁ`.  Without this field the class is strictly weaker than the literature's\n*pivotal*, and Barrett–Westbury does not apply to it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PivotalCategory.pivotor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PivotalCategory.pivotor","kind":"def","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PivotalCategory.lean#L217-L217","doc":"The pivotor: a natural isomorphism identifying each object with its double dual. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PivotalCategory.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PivotalCategory.mk","kind":"ctor","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PivotalCategory.lean#L215-L215","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PivotalCategory","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PivotalCategory","kind":"class","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PivotalCategory.lean#L209-L223","doc":"**A pivotal category**, in the shape Mathlib's \"Future work\" list asks for: a right-rigid\nmonoidal category equipped with a natural isomorphism `𝟭 C ≅ ᘁᘁ`.\n\nThe single field is *data*, not an assertion — the pivotor is a choice, and different choices give\ndifferent (spherical or not) theories.  See `ofPointwise` for the equivalent object-wise\npresentation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.doubleDualFunctor_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.doubleDualFunctor_map","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PivotalCategory.lean#L204-L205","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.doubleDualFunctor_obj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.doubleDualFunctor_obj","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PivotalCategory.lean#L201-L202","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.doubleDualFunctor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.doubleDualFunctor","kind":"def","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PivotalCategory.lean#L193-L199","doc":"**The double-dual endofunctor** `X ↦ Xᘁᘁ`.  Dualising twice is covariant, so this is an\nendofunctor of `C` — the `ᘁᘁ` of Mathlib's pivotal-category TODO. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.rightDualFunctor_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.rightDualFunctor_map","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PivotalCategory.lean#L186-L186","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.rightDualFunctor_obj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.rightDualFunctor_obj","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PivotalCategory.lean#L186-L186","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.rightDualFunctor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.rightDualFunctor","kind":"def","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PivotalCategory.lean#L183-L191","doc":"**Right-dualisation as a functor** `Cᵒᵖ ⥤ C`.  `rightAdjointMate` is contravariant\n(`fᘁ : Yᘁ ⟶ Xᘁ` for `f : X ⟶ Y`), so the source is `Cᵒᵖ`.  This is the functor Mathlib's\n\"Future work\" entry *\"`ᘁ` gives an equivalence of categories `C ≅ (Cᵒᵖ)ᴹᵒᵖ`\"* presupposes. ","signatureChunk":0}]}